 king offered a priceless emerald snake ring from his own finger. Holmes shook his head and held up the portrait instead. \"Your Majesty has something which I should value even more highly. THIS photograph.\"\n\nAnd that was how a great scandal threatened the kingdom of Bohemia, and how the best plans of Mr. Sherlock Holmes were beaten by a woman's wit. He used to make merry over the cleverness of women, but I have not heard him do it lately. When he speaks of Irene Adler, it is always under the honorable title of THE woman.",
